\pard\s2\keepn\sa220\f0\b\fs36 Restore warehouse based order routing\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Prepared 19 October 2026 for the Gluzo middleware maintainers.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb220\sa120\f0\b\fs28 The temporary mode uses the token and configured BCPL location\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 The existing Logix connection will use integration-based order routing until our own Logix system can meet the warehouse-routing contract. We retain both modes so that restoring warehouse matching requires a configuration change and process restart, rather than deleting the temporary implementation or reverting unrelated fixes.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Current settings:\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 ORDER_ROUTING_MODE=integration\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 VINCULUM_LOCATION=PBW\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Integration is the default when ORDER_ROUTING_MODE is absent or blank. The platform API key and integration access token must still pass authentication. The token's integration ID selects an active EasyEcom-to-Vinculum integration; the worker also checks that both platforms remain active. The destination is VINCULUM_LOCATION, shared by eligible integrations in that deployment. No warehouse route row or webhook location attribute selects the destination.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Missing warehouse IDs are accepted in this mode. Provided warehouse fields still undergo normal DTO decoding, including rejection of conflicting warehouse_id and warehouseId values. Order identifiers, customer/address data, items and SKU mappings must still satisfy the existing order-processing rules.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 EASYECOM_LOCATION_KEY is an origin-side location setting. It is separate from Vinculum's PBW code. Stock and shipment schedules still use active configured route locations; this order-routing change does not provision those schedules. Disabled warehouse route rows do not block orders in integration mode. Disable the integration when its order pipeline must be paused.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb220\sa120\f0\b\fs28 Restore warehouse matching when our Logix payloads are ready\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 1. Confirm the future Logix parser emits warehouse_id as its routing-key type and the correct assigned warehouse ID as its value. The current EasyEcom parser accepts warehouse_id or warehouseId. A future source platform needs its own adapter; this switch does not implement a new Logix adapter. Do not substitute import_warehouse_id for the assigned warehouse.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 2. Identify the integration name authenticated by the sender's token. Routes belong to that integration; a row under another integration will not match. Keep the platform key and access token out of this guide and source control.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 3. List and preserve the existing routes, then create any missing active route for every warehouse intended for synchronization. Verify the destination code and origin location key before using the example below.\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 go run ./cmd/gatewayctl integration list\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 go run ./cmd/gatewayctl route list --integration <integration-name>\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 go run ./cmd/gatewayctl route add --integration <integration-name> --type warehouse_id --value 304788 --destination-ref PBW --origin-ref <bcpl-easyecom-location-key>\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 The warehouse ID 304788 was observed in the BCPL callback. Confirm it against the future setup instead of copying it automatically. destination_reference must be the Vinculum orderLocation code. origin_reference is EasyEcom's location_key for the matching warehouse. If the route already exists, inspect it rather than issuing a duplicate add. An existing disabled route can be reactivated after its references have been checked:\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 go run ./cmd/gatewayctl route set-status --id <route-id> --status active\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 4. Pause the sender, let accepted jobs drain, and review failed or resumable workflows before the switch. Events already queued in integration mode carry integration_id routing keys. Warehouse mode will not reinterpret these keys. Workflows that already resolved a route retain that persisted destination when resumed. Do not edit queue messages or state files to force a different destination.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 5. Set the following value in the environment actually used by every intake and worker instance. Rebuild and deploy this change first if the running binary does not yet support the setting. Restart or recreate every instance with the updated environment before re-enabling the sender.\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 ORDER_ROUTING_MODE=warehouse\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Retain VINCULUM_LOCATION for other calls that use the client's default. Warehouse-mode orders use the matched route's destination_reference; they do not fall back to that environment setting. There is no schema migration, and the existing token does not need to be reissued for this mode change.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb220\sa120\f0\b\fs28 Verify both the matching and rejection cases\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Before production cutover, run these repository checks:\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 gofmt -l .\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 go vet ./...\par
\pard\s0\sa55\f1\b0\fs17 go test ./...\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Use new controlled orders for the following staging checks:\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - An authenticated order with a configured warehouse resolves the expected integration, completes ORDER_SYNC, and reaches Vinculum with orderLocation from destination_reference.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - An unconfigured warehouse is SKIPPED at RESOLVE_INTEGRATION. It must not silently use PBW from the environment.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - A route under another integration does not match. Disabled routes and disabled integrations do not resolve through warehouse matching.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - Missing warehouse_id and warehouseId are rejected at intake in warehouse mode. Invalid or revoked credentials still fail authentication.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - A duplicate delivery does not create a second vendor order. Check the vendor order number and location as well as the middleware timeline.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Historical SKIPPED workflows do not automatically restart after a mode change. Simply redelivering an old webhook may return duplicate because its idempotency claim remains. Use a new controlled order for verification. Recover a historical order only through a separately reviewed process that checks whether Vinculum already has it; do not delete claims or rewrite workflow state casually.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb220\sa120\f0\b\fs28 Return to integration mode if warehouse cutover fails\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Pause intake and drain or review work again. Restore ORDER_ROUTING_MODE=integration and confirm VINCULUM_LOCATION=PBW in the BCPL deployment. Restart every intake and worker instance, verify a new controlled order, and then resume the sender. Leave warehouse route rows intact so that the next cutover does not require rebuilding configuration.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 The switch changes order routing only. Continue to manage stock and shipment locations through their existing route configuration in both modes.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb220\sa120\f0\b\fs28 The original implementation remains in the repository\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - app/routing/store.go retains the warehouse-based Resolve method and adds ResolveIntegration for the temporary mode.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - app/routing/integration.go supplies the configured destination for the authenticated integration and enforces the supported platform pair.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - app/config/config.go loads and validates ORDER_ROUTING_MODE.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - cmd/server/main.go selects the matching parser, handler and order resolver.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - app/integrations/easyecom/webhook.go and app/webhook/handler.go accept missing warehouses only when integration routing is explicitly enabled by the server.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 - docs/routing.md describes both modes. This guide is also delivered as the root routing-revert.doc, in Word-compatible RTF format.\par
\pard\s0\sa120\sl264\slmult1\f0\b0\fs22 Keep the warehouse path and its tests while our own Logix integration is being built. A Git revert is not required to restore it. Production acceptance still requires the controlled order checks above; repository tests use stub external APIs and do not prove live BCPL acceptance.\par
}
